Mosquitto on FenrirOS
=====================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is no mosquitto.conf, no
password file and no ACL. Examples are installed next to where they belong:
/etc/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf.example, aclfile.example, pwfile.example,
pskfile.example.

    cp /etc/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf.example /etc/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf
    $EDITOR /etc/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf
    dinitctl enable mosquitto

Mosquitto 2 only listens on localhost until a listener is configured, and
requires `allow_anonymous true` or a password_file/plugin for any listener
that is not local. A minimal network setup:

    listener 1883
    password_file /etc/mosquitto/passwd
    persistence true
    persistence_location /var/lib/mosquitto/

Make the password file with `mosquitto_passwd -c /etc/mosquitto/passwd user`
(chown it to mosquitto). WebSockets listeners (`protocol websockets`) use the
system libwebsockets; the dynamic-security, persist-sqlite and other plugins
are in /usr/lib/mosquitto_*.so. The command-line clients (mosquitto_pub,
mosquitto_sub, mosquitto_rr) are in the mosquitto-clients package.
